meta {
  name: Get Deployment
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/deployments/{{deployment_id}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

params:path {
  deployment_id: 
}

docs {
  # Get Deployment Details
  
  Retrieves complete details about a single deployment including:
  - Deployment metadata and configuration
  - Current status and timestamps
  - Associated template version information
  - OpenStack Heat stack ID (if available)
  - Deployment instances with access URLs
  
  ## Authorization
  - **Lecturer** or **Admin** role required
  - Authorization simplified after removing Course FK
  
  ## Response
  
  Returns deployment with nested objects:
  - `template_version`: Version details and template name
  - `course_id`: Keycloak group ID (string)
  - `instances`: List of VM instances with:
    - Instance name and OpenStack ID
    - Status (ACTIVE, BUILD, etc.)
    - IP address
    - Access URLs (SSH, web, Guacamole, etc.)
  
  ## Example Response
  
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "data": {
      "id": "deploy-123",
      "name": "SQL Kurs - Herbst 2026",
      "template_version_id": "version-456",
      "course_id": "keycloak-group-789",
      "status": "running",
      "openstack_stack_id": "stack-abc",
      "deployment_parameters": "{...}",
      "created_at": "2024-11-27T10:00:00Z",
      "updated_at": "2024-11-27T10:00:00Z",
      "template_version": {
        "id": "version-456",
        "version": "1.0",
        "template_id": "template-abc",
        "template_name": "PostgreSQL Group DB"
      },
      "instances": [
        {
          "id": "instance-123",
          "instance_name": "vm-1",
          "openstack_instance_id": "os-instance-456",
          "status": "ACTIVE",
          "ip_address": "192.168.1.10",
          "access_urls": "{\"ssh\": \"ssh://192.168.1.10\", \"web\": \"http://192.168.1.10\"}",
          "created_at": "2024-11-27T10:05:00Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-11-27T10:05:00Z"
        }
      ]
    },
    "message": "Deployment details retrieved successfully",
    "request_id": "req-456"
  }
  ```
  
  ## Error Responses
  
  **404 Not Found**
  ```json
  {
    "success": false,
    "message": "Deployment with ID xyz not found"
  }
  ```
  
  **403 Forbidden** (if trying to access another lecturer's deployment)
  ```json
  {
    "success": false,
    "message": "You do not have permission to access this deployment"
  }
  ```
}
